## THE GATE'S FINDINGS and TUESDAY'S DECISIONS
Source: `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-02_B1130_STATUS.md` (read whole), `..._B1130_evidence/` (`step4-rail.txt`, `step4-direct-docscroll.txt`, `step5-hover.txt`, `step3-census.txt`, `residue.md`), `..._B1130_ADDENDUM-1_census-second-window_ruling.md`. The gate's scripts are READABLE claims at `.tools/b1130/specs/` (`scroll.cjs` 68 lines, `scrollana.py` 64, `hover.cjs`, `census.cjs` 61, `lib.cjs` 150, `plants.py`): read their headers (`sed -n 1,30p`), never invoke them; **write your own in `.tools/b1190/scratch/`**. Figures are claims; **a "Fix shape" is a proposal: verify first.**
1. **B1130-1 (Blocker), the panel.** Tabbing onto the highlighted (current) menu item within 5 px of the window's top or bottom edge moves the whole PAGE 1 to 5 px: 54 direct document scrolls of 5061 rail trips (partner and admin, 1280 wide, window heights 420 to 900 every 2 px, every rail item, both directions), at 18 item-and-direction spots x 3 heights each (the spots are listed at `step4-rail.txt` and in the STATUS "STEP 4" bullet 2). Downstream, the full sweep reads BROKEN 690 in 432 trips, among them **89 down-then-up trips that leave the page scrolled 52 to 72 px** (or the rail 93 px). Cause (gate's reading): the rail is sticky and `h-dvh` tall (`Sidebar.tsx:68`) but starts one top bar (about 72 px) below the top of the page, so its bottom runs past the window; the `scroll-margin-block: 6px` of the current-item rule (`globals.css:94`) then makes the browser scroll the page as well as the rail. Gate's fix shape: end the rail's scroll box at the window's bottom edge so the 6 px comes from the rail. **The product owner's ruling is that shape: the panel is the height of the space below the top bar.**
2. **B1130-3 (Minor, carried from the round before), the hovered neighbour.** With the NEXT item hovered, the focused current item's bottom edge keeps 2 rows on the middle line (contrast 14.956) in 20 of 32 hovered-next cells (partner Home, My readiness, Customers, Engagements, Delivery phases; 1024 and 1280 wide at 800 tall; both directions); main keeps 3. Gate's fix shape: lift the focused current item above its neighbours (`position: relative` plus `z-index` on the current-item rule, `globals.css:91-95`). **Check what the link already has (`position`, `z-index`) in `GlobalNav.tsx` and `CustomerNav.tsx`, where `sidebar-ring` is applied, before adding anything.**
3. **B1130-2 (Major), the test.** `web/src/components/partner/PartnerDashboard.text.test.tsx:123` (`expect(text).toBe(LOADED)`) and `:134` (`expect(text).toBe(EMPTY)`): `pageText()` (`:109-111`) collapses every run of white space to one space, but the literals `LOADED` (`:22`) and `EMPTY` (`:66`) are compared as written, so **a second space inside the literal's words turns the row red though the page reads the same** (gate plant t5b red; t5a, the layout whitespace between the literal's string pieces, green). Gate's fix shape: collapse the literal the same way (`.replace(/\s+/g, " ")`).
4. **Decisions (Tuesday's, written here):** (i) **no merge or rebase of main** (D-1 below); (ii) the **trip census is YOUR evidence** that the jump is 0 (D-2); (iii) the hovered-neighbour and the scroll fixes get **one browser row each**, red at the old head (D-3); (iv) a panel-height shape that needs `AppShell.tsx`, a script, JS, padding, font-size or a word: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the candidates table (D-4).

